# Cloudflare Pages header rules — the (hardening) snippet from the app repo's
# ansible/templates/caddy.j2, reproduced for the Pages edge now that Caddy no
# longer serves this host. Astro copies public/ verbatim into dist/, which is
# what Pages parses; this file is never served as an asset.
#
# Deliberately NOT reproduced from (hardening):
#   -Server            Cloudflare always sends `Server: cloudflare`. Nothing
#                      leaks — it names the CDN, not our software.
#   encode gzip zstd   Cloudflare negotiates gzip/brotli on its own.
#   log -> fail2ban    there is no origin left to jail.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-XSS-Protection: 1; mode=block
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload

# The pages.dev alias stays reachable — it is what docs.pglantern.com CNAMEs to
# and the rollback target if the custom domain misbehaves — but it must never
# compete with the real host in search results. astro.config.mjs' `site:`
# already emits canonical links; this is the belt-and-braces. _headers matches
# absolute URLs, so this rule is scoped to the alias alone.
https://horton-docs.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
